  "question": {
    "text": "The number of electrons flowing per second in the filament of a $110 \\mathrm{~W}$ bulb operating at $220 \\mathrm{~V}$ is : $\\left(\\right.$ Given $\\left.\\mathrm{e}=1.6 \\times 10^{-19} \\mathrm{C}\\right)$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$6.25 \\times 10^{17}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$1.25 \\times 10^{19}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$6.25 \\times 10^{18}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$31.25 \\times 10^{17}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Power $(\\mathrm{P})=\\mathrm{V} . \\mathrm{I}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow 110=(220)(\\mathrm{I}) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{I}=0.5 \\mathrm{~A}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Now, $I=\\frac{n \\cdot e}{t}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow 0.5=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{\\mathrm{t}}\\right)\\left(1.6 \\times 10^{-19}\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{\\mathrm{t}}=\\frac{0.5}{1.6 \\times 10^{-19}} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{\\mathrm{t}}=31.25 \\times 10^{17}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}